 ### Changed
 
+- A subagent never takes the parent's model, the session model or the `default` role, and it runs on exactly one model for its whole life. Every spawn without a per-call, host or seance model, from the task tool or from eval `agent()`/`workpool()`, goes through automatic model selection. One usable role alias is chosen without the judge (`only one configured alias`); two or more go to the judge, and a judge that fails, times out or is not confident chooses nothing (there is no fallback role). When selection cannot choose, a `task.agentModelOverrides` entry or the agent's own `model` is used with a visible warning (a notice, a warning line on the subagent row and a `<model-warning>` in the result); with neither, the spawn fails before the child starts and the error tells the parent agent to stop and report to you instead of changing settings.
+- A subagent no longer falls back to the parent's model when its own model has no working credentials, and it no longer inherits the `default` or a role fallback chain. Only a chain you wrote in `retry.fallbackChains` under the exact `provider/model-id` it runs on can move it, and using it raises the same warning. A task result whose child ended on another model than it started on says so in a `<model-warning>`.
+- `task.prewalk`, `task.agentPrewalk` and an agent's `prewalk` frontmatter no longer apply to subagents: a subagent never hands off to another model. Session-level prewalk is unchanged.
 - `omp update` and the startup update check now use the latest stable release of the fork's GitHub repository (`kierandrewett/omp`, versions like `18.14.2-fork.1`): the `omp-linux-x64` asset is checked against `SHA256SUMS.txt` before it replaces the running binary, and the previous binary is restored if the new one fails version verification. `PI_BUILD_URL` and the upstream npm registry are no longer consulted, and npm, bun, Homebrew, mise and Nix installs are not updated from here.
 
